-- title:
--   Maximal growth passes to the degree-m part of J+(ℓ)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$ and $m$ with $m \ge 1$, a field $k$, and write $S = k[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ for the polynomial ring in $n+1$ variables indexed by `Fin (n+1)`. For an ideal $I$ of $S$ and a degree $d$, `piece I d` denotes the quotient of the $k$-module of polynomials homogeneous of degree $d$ by the submodule of those lying in $I$, so that $\dim_k$ `piece I d` is the value $h_I(d)$ of the Hilbert function of $S/I$ at $d$; [`Nat.macaulayPow m a`](def/Nat_MacaulayPow.html#L7) is Macaulay's pseudo-power $a^{\langle m\rangle}$, given by the recursion displayed in its definition. Let $J$ be an ideal of $S$ that is the ideal generated by some set of polynomials each homogeneous of degree $m$, let $a : \mathrm{Fin}(n+1) \to k$ and put $\ell = \sum_j a_j x_j$. Assume the two numerical hypotheses $h_{J+(\ell)}(m+1) = h_{J+(\ell)}(m)^{\langle m\rangle}$ and $h_{J+(\ell)}(m)^{\langle m\rangle} + h_J(m) = h_J(m)^{\langle m\rangle}$, where $J+(\ell)$ is the join of $J$ with the ideal generated by $\ell$. Let $J'$ be the ideal generated by the set of polynomials that both lie in $J+(\ell)$ and are homogeneous of degree $m$. Then $h_{J'}(m+1) = h_{J'}(m)^{\langle m\rangle}$, and if $h_J(m) > 0$ then $h_{J'}(m) < h_J(m)$.
--
--   This is the Green–Gotzmann step which replaces $J$ by the ideal generated by the degree-$m$ forms of $J + (\ell)$: the new ideal still grows maximally from degree $m$ to degree $m+1$ in the sense of Macaulay's pseudo-power, while its degree-$m$ Hilbert value strictly drops. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_linearForm_section_maximal_growth`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_linearForm_section_maximal_growth) in the construction of a linear form along which Hilbert-function growth is maximal, part of the numerical control of Hilbert functions underlying the Hilbert functor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_finrank_piece_span_sup_linearForm_eq_macaulayPow_and_lt.lean

